    <briefdescription>
<para>Carries named field references for wall-function boundary conditions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Wall functions that need auxiliary fields (U, nu, nearWallDist, omega, k …) look up what they need by name instead of accepting a fixed argument list. All fields are stored as non-owning const pointers; the caller is responsible for ensuring the lifetime of the referenced fields exceeds the context. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
